<title>BELGIUM: Commission strikes veterinary trade deal with Czechs.</title>
<headline>Commission strikes veterinary trade deal with Czechs.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had concluded a draft agreement with the Czech Republic on the mutual recognition of veterinary, plant health and animal welfare trading standards.</p>
<p>The accord has to be approved by the EU countries.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Prague will gradually bring its rules into line with those of the EU in preparation for its membership of the 15-nation bloc.</p>
<p>&quot;The draft agreement has the double aim of boosting trade and creating a climate of mutual confidence,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>In December the EU signed a similar agreement with New Zealand. In March it reached agreement in principle with Canada and on April 30 it sealed a deal with the United States on red meat, dairy and fish products.</p>
</text>
